ARTICLE II
Preconditions
1. The Government of the United States of America shall propose, in its sole discretion, to the Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde, through the usual diplomatic channels, the transfer of third-country nationals who have, by the time of their transfer, sought protection against return to their country of origin or former habitual residence;
2. The Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde shall in its complete discretion consider accepting or denying in whole or in part a proposal made by the Government of the United States of America in accordance with paragraph 1, and based on the criteria established in operating procedures developed pursuant to Article IV;
3. For each third-country national proposed for transfer, the Government of the United States of America shall provide documentation, including but not limited to identity documentation and biographic data, to the extent such documentation exists and is in the possession of the Government of the United States of America and to the extent permitted by law, consistent with the operating procedures developed pursuant to Article IV;
4. For each third-country national proposed for transfer, the Government of the United States of America shall provide documentation, including but not limited to identity documentation, biographic data, criminal records (if applicable), and other relevant documents in its possession, to the extent such documentation exists and is in the possession of the United States of America, and to the extent permitted by law, consistent with the operating procedures developed pursuant to Article IV;
5. The Government of the United States of America shall not propose to the Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde the transfer of third-country

in operating procedures developed pursuant to Article IV, and subject to the number of third-country national transfers outlined in operating procedures developed pursuant to Article IV, and the Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde agrees to make a decision regarding the Government of the United States of America's proposed transfers on the timeline identified in operating procedures developed pursuant to Article IV;
3. The Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde shall create the humane conditions necessary for receiving and facilitating the process of social integration, pursuant to its international obligations, national legislation, social policies, and the terms of this Agreement;
4. The Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde agrees not to send any individual transferred from the United States of America pursuant to this Agreement to his or her country of origin or nationality or former habitual residence, except in cases in which a final decision has been made relating to any pending claims for protection;
5. The Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde shall establish procedures, consistent with the terms of this Agreement and its international obligations and national legislation, to resolve the status of individuals who fail to seek protection or withdraw pending claims or petitions for protection in Cabo Verde; and
6. The Government of the United States of America, upon request, shall endeavor, in accordance with applicable law and regulations, to provide financial and technical assistance to strengthen the institutional capacities of the Government of the Republic of Cabo Verde for the reception and integration of the individuals transferred under this Agreement.

